---
---

<section class="section my-0! py-10 relative z-0 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="container">
    <hgroup class="text-center max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2>
        What <span
          class="bg-linear-to-r from-[#0179B4] to-[#88D8FF] bg-clip-text text-transparent"
          >we actually do</span
        >
      </h2>
      <p>
        We are a placement and contract staffing network, not a clinic. Year one
        is deliberately narrow: we move African healthcare professionals into
        hospitals that have vacancies they cannot fill.
      </p>
    </hgroup>

    <div class="relative grid gap-10 grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 mt-10 max-w-6xl mx-auto after:absolute after:-top-5 after:-left-10 after:bg-[url('/img/shape/shape2.svg')] after:bg-no-repeat after:w-35.5 after:h-9.25 after:bg-position-[left_top] after:bg-contain after:z-0

	before:absolute before:-bottom-5 before:-right-10 before:bg-[url('/img/shape/shape2-1.svg')] before:bg-no-repeat before:w-35.5 before:h-9.25 before:bg-position-[right_bottom] before:bg-contain before:z-0">
      <article
        class="lg:col-span-2 border-2 border-main-200 rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-10 bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black"
      >
        <svg class="icon" width="44" height="44">
          <use xlink:href="#i1"></use>
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-main-200 mt-3">Permanent placement</h3>
        <p>
          Nurses, doctors, midwives and paramedics sourced from Ghana, Nigeria,
          Kenya and elsewhere in Africa, matched to permanent hospital and
          clinic roles in Europe, the United States and the Gulf. We handle
          sourcing, credentialing and the destination paperwork; the hospital
          hires the clinician directly.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="border-2 border-main-200 rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-10 bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black"
      >
        <svg class="icon" width="44" height="44">
          <use xlink:href="#i2"></use>
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-main-200 mt-3">Contract and rotational staffing</h3>
        <p>
          Fixed-term and rotational cover for wards that cannot wait for a
          permanent hire, including agency-style block contracts.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="border-2 border-main-200 rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-10 bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black"
      >
        <svg class="icon" width="44" height="44">
          <use xlink:href="#i3"></use>
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-main-200 mt-3">Credentialing and licensing</h3>
        <p>
          Registration checked against the home-country council, then mapped to
          the destination regulator&rsquo;s requirements &mdash; the part that
          decides whether a placement is real or not.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="border-2 border-main-200 rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-10 bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black"
      >
        <svg class="icon" width="44" height="44">
          <use xlink:href="#i4"></use>
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-main-200 mt-3">Employer recruitment</h3>
        <p>
          Hospitals and health groups tell us the role, the grade and the
          destination market. We return shortlists against that brief, not a
          general directory.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="border-2 border-main-200 rounded-xl p-4 lg:p-10 bg-[linear-gradient(45deg,#F8FDFF,#FFFFFF)] text-black"
      >
        <svg class="icon" width="44" height="44">
          <use xlink:href="#i5"></use>
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-main-200 mt-3">Public clinician profiles</h3>
        <p>
          Every clinician holds a permanent address at
          <code>/profilename</code> carrying their verified record &mdash;
          checkable by an employer without an introduction.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>